"/bin/zsh -lc \"codex exec --sandbox read-only --ephemeral --skip-git-repo-check --output-schema <(printf '%s' '{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"},\\\"findings\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"array\\\",\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\"}}},\\\"required\\\":[\\\"verdict\\\",\\\"findings\\\"],\\\"additionalProperties\\\":false}') 'Independently review this Storybloq setup proposal against brief.md. Read only; make no writes. Check coverage, fidelity, journey completeness, dependencies, usability, domain rules, risks and verifiable acceptance. No implementation is requested.\nProject Plotbook is brief-only, stack/type/language undecided (generic until owner selects). No capabilities complete. First version covers all five numbered requirements, all rules and mobile/privacy/plain-language constraints. Payments and tool lending deferred.\nEach implementation ticket will have Outcome with brief heading citation, Scope and Excludes, observable Acceptance, Behaviour (loading/empty/errors/recovery/accessibility), Verification, Prerequisites and Assumptions.\nProposed milestones and dependencies (local labels, not allocated ticket IDs):\nA Decisions and early prototype: D1 owner checkpoint choose sign-in and household identity, report notification inclusion/channel, season date interpretation and application cutoff timezone/boundary, returning priority versus strictly chronological waitlist, stack/deployment and actual 40-plot layout. Decisions may be split and unrelated work proceed. A1 phone prototype using synthetic data for apply (up to three preferences), allocation/queue, own allocation, problem reporting and map. A2 Checkpoint review prototype for plain language, large text and usable journey, depends A1. Prototype tool is owner choice/TBD; no stack invented.\nB Foundation/intake: B1 scaffold chosen stack and establish test/build commands, depends stack portion D1. B2 season/40 plots/households/application model and persistence (March-October, previous holders, unique household-season allocation, exclusive plot-season holding), depends B1 and relevant domain D1. B3 sign-in/role permissions protecting contact fields on server, own-household access, coordinator-only allocation/contacts; depends B2 and identity D1. B4 phone application intake and coordinator application review, validate <=3 distinct existing preferences, preserve application ordering, avoid duplicate submissions, depends B3,A2. B5 Checkpoint demonstrate signed-in application and privacy depends B4.\nC Allocation: C1 allocation eligibility/order core with returning-before-new for prior-season holders applied before Feb 1, guard one household plot/season and prevent double-booking under concurrency; depends B2 and priority/cutoff decisions D1. C2 coordinator allocation workflow and chronological waiting list, atomic save/conflict refresh, depends C1,B4,A2. C3 gardener own allocation/season dates/unallocated state depends C2,B3. C4 coordinator grid of all 40 plots with holders and vacancies plus readable phone/list alternative, depends C2,A2 and layout D1. C5 Checkpoint demonstrate priority, queue, allocation and map depends C2,C3,C4.\nD Problems and acceptance: D2 gardener submits report for own allocated plot and gets confirmation/retry, depends C3,A2. D3 coordinator open problem list, detail, resolve, empty/errors and authorization; depends D2. D4 conditional notification ticket only if owner opts in; otherwise record explicit deferral, depends D3 and notification decision. D5 integrated rule/privacy/accessibility checks and first-version verification using synthetic households, cutoff tests, competing allocations, chronological queue, phones, large text, keyboard/screen-reader and recoverable failures, depends B5,C5,D3 (and D4 if included). D6 Checkpoint owner accepts all five brief outcomes and rules depends D5.\nCoverage: req1 B4; req2 C1/C2; req3 C3; req4 D2/D3 (notification unresolved); req5 C4; rules B2/C1/C2; constraints A1/A2/B3/D5. Optional notification and stack unresolved, not silently selected. All early domain derivations labelled assumptions awaiting owner; no invented research, performance targets, or exact season dates.\nPackage also proposes AGENTS.md, RULES.md (TDD for business logic), REVIEW.md verbatim skill contract, git init and ignores .story/snapshots/, .story/sessions/, .story/status.json. Full pipeline because allocation rules/workflows. WRITE_TESTS/TEST/BUILD/VERIFY explicitly disabled pending real manifest commands; no installs/builds/tests during setup. Owner checkpoints are ordinary tickets with no enforced gating. No writes until user approves concrete package. Give concise findings and verdict.'\""
